# Screens that differ on purpose: screen (the picture's name)<TAB>reason. compare.py reports them as expected, and as stale when they match after all.	
administrator-wp-admin-site-health-php	Site Health's tests report the server: PHP-only checks and sections are not ported (HyScribe has its own Info section, no PHP version, scheduled event or inactive plugin checks)
administrator-wp-admin-site-health-php-tab-debug	Site Health's Info lists PHP's server, constants, directories and plugin sections; HyScribe's list is its own, and its results still load
administrator-wp-admin-post-new-php-post-type-page	The block patterns list answers 501 (it fetches the wordpress.org pattern directory, an open question), so the editor shows no start patterns dialog
administrator-wp-admin-post-new-php	The block patterns list answers 501, and so does the write of the user's persisted editor preferences (POST users/me)
editor-wp-admin-post-new-php	The block patterns list answers 501, and so does the write of the user's persisted editor preferences (POST users/me)
administrator-wp-admin-post-php-post-1-action-edit	The write of the user's persisted editor preferences (POST users/me) answers 501
administrator-wp-admin-site-editor-php	The navigation fallback route answers 501: PHP writes a wp_navigation post there, which HyScribe does not
administrator-wp-admin-upload-php-mode-grid	The URL prefix (ADR 0008): the grid's Backbone router matches upload.php, which hs-admin prints as upload, so its address stays upload?mode=grid
